# Rust build artifacts
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Phase-6.0-W4: LLVM coverage raw/merged profiles (cargo-llvm-cov writes
# `*.profraw` via LLVM_PROFILE_FILE; if a run is invoked from a crate
# subdir they can land outside /target). Never tracked — pure coverage
# build artifacts; the tracked ratchet state is `coverage-floors.toml`.
**/*.profraw
**/*.profdata

# Cargo.lock IS tracked — this workspace produces a binary (`fsm`).

# OS / editor metadata
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Generated code dropped by `fsm generate` during dogfood runs
/generated/
examples/*/generated/

# Snapshot test pending files
**/*.snap.new
**/*.pending-snap

# VS Code extension (v1.3, Doc 28 §2 Option A): node_modules + the esbuild
# output live under editors/vscode/ and are NOT tracked; the
# @vscode/test-electron VS Code download goes to its default OUT-OF-TREE
# cache (~/.vscode-test), never under /root/dev — the cargo-target
# out-of-tree posture (.cargo/config.toml) applied to the Node toolchain so
# the cold-cargo disk trough is never worsened by JS caches.
editors/vscode/node_modules/
editors/vscode/out/
editors/vscode/dist/
editors/vscode/.vscode-test/
editors/vscode/*.vsix
# Phase-6.0-W4: the c8 coverage report + V8 temp profiles are build
# artifacts. The TRACKED ratchet state is `.c8rc.json` (its thresholds +
# the recorded measured numbers in its "//floors" key); the report dir is
# regenerated by `npm run test:coverage`. Never tracked.
editors/vscode/coverage/

# V6 bundled host-triple binaries (Doc 28 §3-V6). `bin/<host-triple>/`
# holds the ~12 MB release `fsm` + `fsm-lang-server` the VSIX packages and
# V1's Rule-2 resolver loads. It is a BUILD ARTIFACT produced fresh by
# `scripts/populate-bin.mjs` at package time — committing a native binary
# to git is a cardinal repo-bloat sin (the brief's hard NO-HUGE-BINARIES
# discipline). NOT tracked; rebuilt deterministically on the pinned 1.75.
editors/vscode/bin/

# Python bytecode (scripts/coverage-gate.py compile cache)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
